        "self_reported": {
          "assumptions": [
            "clip.exe takes UTF-16LE through iconv and explorer.exe opens the WSL directory it is started in; built without a WSL machine to run them on",
            "bale's base check at apply will catch, not silently merge, a response that rewrites a folder.md the office recorded a session in after packing"
          ],
          "judgment_calls": [
            "the opener is read from between the scissor lines bale prints on stderr, the block bale asks a person to copy, because the --json report carries none; filed as a slip for bale-src",
            "office start checks the planned forecast against bale status --json before packing and refuses plainly, naming the open session and its folder",
            "context packs run before the session pack, so a failure there opens nothing; the doctrine and any plain-directory ride-along are packed from scratch copies so the install and the occupant's directories are never written",
            "a ride-along inside a repo is packed from the repo's top with --include (bale's outbox there is ignored); a file outside any repo is copied into the tray as it is",
            "an office session about a project (its folder's lane names one) carries that project's tree and declared ride-alongs as context",
            "an office session's default slug gets -office, because bale's ids are unique per repo and the same folder packed in the office and a project the same day would mint one id twice",
            "the out tray is ~/out-tray/SID unless machine.toml in the per-machine config directory says otherwise; on WSL the clipboard and Explorer steps default on",
            "office slip's about is one word: office, bale, office-src, a project, or any other tool name; piped and untold it writes no about line and says so",
